 "kind": "trial",
 "note": "Guarded quadratic (degree-reduced) fast path in eik_tanh_r cells_ for tld_r rows 0..27 (t in [0x7B201000,0x7C..), c1!=0): drops the c3*t cubic term via per-row precomputed c2' = c2 + mulhsx(c3, cell-centre t) (new 28-entry int32 table tq_r, 112 bytes), keeps the high-half multiply formulation, returns w-(Vq>>8) only when Vq mod 256 lies in an exhaustively proven window (even rows [4,213], odd rows [44,253]) so the cubic would return the identical value; otherwise falls through to the unchanged cubic/refinement. Result: rv32im S regresses (see ratios); thumbv6m code generation unchanged.",
